{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.04}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Damaged cards will be replaced free of charge, but there is a fee to replace a lost card\" leaves unclear which rule governs a card that is both lost and later returned damaged. The boundary between \"lost\" and \"damaged\" is not defined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.04}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The enumerated privileges (check cashing, elections, athletic events, library, campus technologies) are followed by \"etc.\", leaving the reach of the catch-all uncertain, and \"properly entitled\" is nowhere defined. A student and the University could reasonably differ on what falls inside the list.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Encouraging, enticing, influencing, or enlisting\" another student is undefined, and \"influencing\" in particular has no ascertainable boundary. Ordinary conversation could fall within it on one reading.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.07}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Maintain currency with the use of the University-issued e-mail account\" states no frequency or standard, and the following sentence (\"communicating information important requests, updates\") is garbled by a missing word or punctuation. What the student actually must do is therefore uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
   {"issue": "This provision underpins the notice mechanism in Section 19.1 and 19.6 (charges and hearing notice delivered to the Brandeis e-mail account), but it imposes no clear duty that would make such delivery effective notice.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The prohibited behaviours are listed as bare verbs — \"intimidates\", \"threatens\", \"harasses or bullies\", \"invades personal privacy\", \"unwanted physical contact\", \"endangers the health, safety, or welfare\" — with no definitions or intent element. These are the charging standards for discipline and each is reasonably susceptible of narrow and broad readings.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.55},
   {"issue": "The final sentence permits emergency suspension of any student \"involved in such an incident\" pending investigation, while Section 22.2 permits altering a student's status only for \"reasons of imminent danger\". The two cannot easily be read together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
   {"issue": "A duty to \"comply with instructions of University officials, committees, or boards\" is unlimited in subject matter and contains no reasonableness or scope qualifier. Whether it reaches any instruction whatever is genuinely open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
   {"issue": "\"Dean's Action\" is used here as a defined-sounding term but Section 22 speaks of \"Dean's Actions and Sanctions\" without defining \"Dean's Action\" as such. The referent is left to inference.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Obstructing or disrupting ... administrative, public service, disciplinary, or other authorized functions\" ends in an open catch-all whose reach beyond the enumerated functions is uncertain. \"Legitimate functions\" is itself undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Causes disruption to\" and \"invades another individual's privacy\" are undefined and the sentence's grammar leaves it unclear whether \"in a classroom, library or other campus facility\" qualifies both verbs. The scope of the prohibition therefore shifts with the reading.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.07}
